.TH PAVUCLI 1 "2026-11-16" "pavucli 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pavucli \- terminal volume control for PulseAudio and PipeWire
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pavucli
[\fB\-t\fR \fITAB\fR] [\fB\-s\fR \fIPCT\fR] [\fB\-m\fR \fIPCT\fR] [\fB\-\-ascii\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-mouse\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pavucli
is a curses mixer in the spirit of
.BR pavucontrol (1).
It shows playback and recording streams, output and input devices and sound card
profiles, and lets you change volume, per\-channel volume, balance and mute state,
move streams between devices, select ports, pick the default device and switch
card profiles. It talks to the server through
.BR pactl (1)
and refreshes automatically when anything changes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-tab " " \fITAB\fR
Tab to open: playback, recording, output, input or config.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-step " " \fIPCT\fR
Volume step of the arrow keys in percent (default 5).
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-max\-volume " " \fIPCT\fR
Upper end of the volume bars, 100\-400 percent (default 150).
.TP
.B \-\-ascii
Draw with plain ASCII characters.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable colours. Also enabled by a non\-empty \fBNO_COLOR\fR variable.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-mouse
Do not capture the mouse (keeps the terminal's own text selection).
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Tab, Shift\-Tab, F1\-F5
Switch tabs.
.TP
.B Up/Down, k/j, Home/End
Select an item.
.TP
.B Left/Right, h/l
Volume down/up by the step. \fBH\fR/\fBL\fR or Shift+arrows: 1 %. PgDn/PgUp: 10 %.
.TP
.B 1 ... 9, 0
Set volume to 10 % ... 90 %, 0 sets 100 %.
.TP
.B m
Toggle mute.
.TP
.B [ ]
Shift balance left / right; \fBb\fR or \fB=\fR centres it.
.TP
.B c, Space
Lock/unlock channels to adjust each channel separately.
.TP
.B Enter
Streams: move to another device. Devices: choose port. Configuration: choose profile.
.TP
.B p
Choose the port of a device.
.TP
.B d
Make the selected device the default output/input.
.TP
.B M
Show or hide monitor sources on the Input Devices tab.
.TP
.B ?
Help.
.TP
.B q, Esc
Quit.
.PP
With the mouse, click a tab or an item, click inside a volume bar to set the
volume, and use the wheel to change the volume of the item under the pointer.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.BR pactl (1)
from libpulse 16 or newer (JSON output), and a running PulseAudio or
pipewire\-pulse server.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pactl (1),
.BR pavucontrol (1),
.BR wpctl (1)
